{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/fred2005-formal-groups/blocks/def-unit-root-f-crystal","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:unit-root-f-crystal","kind":"definition","title":"Unit-root F-crystal","uses":["papers/fred2005-formal-groups/blocks/def-commutative-formal-group"],"cites":["references/hazewinkel1978","references/zink2002"],"tags":["f-crystal","unit-root","frobenius"],"leanRef":"fred2005:Fred2005.UnitRootFCrystal","text":"unit-root-f-crystal.md","leanSource":"folio/fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/unit-root-f-crystal.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:unit-root-f-crystal\"></a><p>A <strong>unit-root F-crystal</strong> on a\n<a href=\"#def:commutative-formal-group\">commutative formal group</a> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H</code> is an\nF-crystal whose Frobenius endomorphism acts invertibly (bijectively)\non the coordinate ring <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{O}(H)</code>.  The unit-root condition\nmeans there is no nilpotent part in the Dieudonne--Manin decomposition.</p>\n<p>Reference: <span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"hazewinkel1978\">[hazewinkel1978]</span>, Chapter V; <span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"zink2002\">[zink2002]</span>, Section 2.</p>\n","source":"folio/fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/unit-root-f-crystal.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Definition","number":"1.7.1"}
